      {
        "question_text": "[tikz]\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\\normalsize}]\n\\usetikzlibrary{arrows.meta}\n\\draw[black,{Stealth}-{Stealth}] (-0.3,0)--(9.4,0);\n\\draw[black] (0,-0.08)--(0,0.08);\\node[below] at (0,-0.16) {$0$};\n\\draw[black] (1,-0.08)--(1,0.08);\\node[below] at (1,-0.16) {$10$};\n\\draw[black] (2,-0.08)--(2,0.08);\\node[below] at (2,-0.16) {$20$};\n\\draw[black] (3,-0.08)--(3,0.08);\\node[below] at (3,-0.16) {$30$};\n\\draw[black] (4,-0.08)--(4,0.08);\\node[below] at (4,-0.16) {$40$};\n\\draw[black] (5,-0.08)--(5,0.08);\\node[below] at (5,-0.16) {$50$};\n\\draw[black] (6,-0.08)--(6,0.08);\\node[below] at (6,-0.16) {$60$};\n\\draw[black] (7,-0.08)--(7,0.08);\\node[below] at (7,-0.16) {$70$};\n\\draw[black] (8,-0.08)--(8,0.08);\\node[below] at (8,-0.16) {$80$};\n\\draw[black] (9,-0.08)--(9,0.08);\\node[below] at (9,-0.16) {$90$};\n\\node[below] at (4.5,-0.65) {Score (marks)};\n\\draw[black,thick] (1.70,1.4)--(3.30,1.4);\n\\draw[black,thick] (6.90,1.4)--(8.60,1.4);\n\\draw[black,thick] (1.70,1.2)--(1.70,1.6);\n\\draw[black,thick] (8.60,1.2)--(8.60,1.6);\n\\draw[black,thick] (3.30,1.0) rectangle (6.90,1.8);\n\\draw[black,thick] (5.10,1.0)--(5.10,1.8);\n\\node[above] at (1.70,1.95) {$17$};\n\\node[above] at (3.30,1.95) {$33$};\n\\node[above] at (5.10,1.95) {$51$};\n\\node[above] at (6.90,1.95) {$69$};\n\\node[above] at (8.60,1.95) {$86$};\n\\end{tikzpicture}\n[/tikz]\nA test was taken by $156$ students. The box plot summarises their scores.\n(a) Between which scores is the middle $50\\%$ of the data?\n(b) Estimate the percentage who scored above $69$.\n(c) Estimate the percentage who scored below $69$.\n(d) Estimate how many scored below $69$.",
        "solution_text": "The box edges give $Q_1=33$ and $Q_3=69$; the line inside gives the median, $51$.\n\n[tikz]\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\\fontsize{10}{12}\\selectfont}]\n\\draw[thick] (1.7,0.4)--(3.3,0.4);\n\\draw[thick] (6.9,0.4)--(8.6,0.4);\n\\draw[thick] (1.7,0.2)--(1.7,0.6);\n\\draw[thick] (8.6,0.2)--(8.6,0.6);\n\\draw[thick,fill=none] (3.3,0) rectangle (6.9,0.8);\n\\draw[thick] (5.1,0)--(5.1,0.8);\n\\node[above] at (1.7,0.9) {$17$};\n\\node[above] at (3.3,0.9) {$Q_1=33$};\n\\node[above] at (5.1,0.9) {Median $51$};\n\\node[above] at (6.9,0.9) {$Q_3=69$};\n\\node[above] at (8.6,0.9) {$86$};\n\\node[below] at (2.5,-0.15) {$25\\%$};\n\\node[below] at (4.2,-0.15) {$25\\%$};\n\\node[below] at (6,-0.15) {$25\\%$};\n\\node[below] at (7.75,-0.15) {$25\\%$};\n\\end{tikzpicture}\n[/tikz]\n\n(a) The middle $50\\%$ lies in the box, between **$33$ and $69$**.\n\n(b) Above $Q_3$ is one quarter: **about $25\\%$**.\n\n(c) Below $Q_3$ are three quarters: $3\\times25\\%=75\\%$, so **about $75\\%$**.\n\n(d) Estimated number:\n$\\begin{aligned}&\\mathrel{\\phantom{=}}0.75\\times156\\\\&=117\\end{aligned}$\n\nAbout **$117$ students**."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "The box plot summarises the lengths of $120$ babies born at a hospital.\n\n[tikz]\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\\fontsize{10}{12}\\selectfont}]\n\\draw[->] (-0.3,0)--(6.4,0);\n\\foreach \\x/\\v in {0/32,1/37,2/42,3/47,4/52,5/57,6/62}{\\draw (\\x,-0.08)--(\\x,0.08);\\node[below,font=\\fontsize{8.5}{10}\\selectfont] at (\\x,-0.12) {$\\v$};}\n\\node[below] at (3,-0.6) {Length (cm)};\n\\draw[thick] (0,1.1)--(2,1.1);\n\\draw[thick] (4,1.1)--(6,1.1);\n\\draw[thick] (0,0.9)--(0,1.3);\n\\draw[thick] (6,0.9)--(6,1.3);\n\\draw[thick,fill=none] (2,0.7) rectangle (4,1.5);\n\\draw[thick] (3,0.7)--(3,1.5);\n\\end{tikzpicture}\n[/tikz]\n\n(a) Between which lengths does the lowest $50\\%$ lie?\n(b) Below which length does approximately $75\\%$ lie?\n(c) Above which length does approximately $25\\%$ lie?\n(d) Estimate the percentage with lengths between $42$ cm and $52$ cm.\n(e) Estimate how many babies are shorter than $42$ cm.\n(f) Estimate how many babies have lengths between $47$ cm and $52$ cm.\n(g) Estimate how many babies have lengths between $42$ cm and $52$ cm.",
        "solution_text": "[tikz]\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\\fontsize{10}{12}\\selectfont}]\n\\draw[thick] (0,0.4)--(2,0.4);\n\\draw[thick] (4,0.4)--(6,0.4);\n\\draw[thick] (0,0.2)--(0,0.6);\n\\draw[thick] (6,0.2)--(6,0.6);\n\\draw[thick,fill=none] (2,0) rectangle (4,0.8);\n\\draw[thick] (3,0)--(3,0.8);\n\\node[above] at (0,0.9) {$32$};\n\\node[above] at (2,0.9) {$42$};\n\\node[above] at (3,0.9) {$47$};\n\\node[above] at (4,0.9) {$52$};\n\\node[above] at (6,0.9) {$62$};\n\\node[below] at (1,-0.15) {$25\\%$};\n\\node[below] at (2.5,-0.15) {$25\\%$};\n\\node[below] at (3.5,-0.15) {$25\\%$};\n\\node[below] at (5,-0.15) {$25\\%$};\n\\end{tikzpicture}\n[/tikz]\n\nThe minimum is $32$ cm, $Q_1=42$ cm, the median is $47$ cm and $Q_3=52$ cm.\n\n(a) The lowest half runs from the minimum to the median: **$32$ cm to $47$ cm**.\n\n(b) Three quarters lie below $Q_3$: **$52$ cm**.\n\n(c) The upper quarter lies above $Q_3$: **$52$ cm**.\n\n(d) The whole box contains two quarters: **about $50\\%$**.\n\n(e) Below $Q_1$ is one quarter.\n$\\begin{aligned}&\\mathrel{\\phantom{=}}0.25\\times120\\\\&=30\\end{aligned}$\n\nAbout **$30$ babies**.\n\n(f) Between the median and $Q_3$ is one quarter.\n$\\begin{aligned}&\\mathrel{\\phantom{=}}0.25\\times120\\\\&=30\\end{aligned}$\n\nAbout **$30$ babies**.\n\n(g) Between $Q_1$ and $Q_3$ is half the dataset.\n$\\begin{aligned}&\\mathrel{\\phantom{=}}0.5\\times120\\\\&=60\\end{aligned}$\n\nAbout **$60$ babies**."
      }
    ],
